# DRAFT-J2CLI-CPYTHON312-CLI-CONTRACT
# Legacy Python CLIs must replace removed imp APIs and test their installed console entry point

id:                     DRAFT-J2CLI-CPYTHON312-CLI-CONTRACT
trigger_tool:           python|conan|test|runtime
phase:                  compilation|installation|testing|runtime
error_signature:        No module named ['"]imp['"]|AttributeError: .*readfp|ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ['"]jinja2['"]|j2 --version
severity:               2
category:               python, compat, portability, ohos, testing
match_keywords:         imp, importlib.util, ConfigParser.readfp, Python 3.12, console_scripts, j2cli:main, PYTHONPATH, unittest
                         Jinja2, PyYAML, entry point

title:                  HarmonyOS Python 3.12+ CLI ports must replace removed APIs and verify the installed entry point

root_cause:             Python 3.12 removes the legacy imp module, while older CLIs can also rely on removed ConfigParser.readfp
                         and pkg_resources supplied incidentally by setuptools. Import-only or source-tree tests can miss these
                         runtime failures and a broken console entry point. j2cli 0.3.12b exercised this boundary on HarmonyOS
                         PC Python 3.14.7: migration to importlib.util, ConfigParser.read_file, explicit version metadata, and
                         execution of the packaged j2 command restored the documented upstream invocation.
affected_scope:         Pure-Python CLI packages whose upstream source or tests load plugins/filters with imp, use removed
                         ConfigParser APIs, or rely on undeclared setuptools runtime imports; validated with j2cli v0.3.12b.
verification_cmd:       python3 -c 'import imp' should fail on CPython 3.12+; after port run the complete upstream unittest suite,
                         install/package the declared console_scripts target, then invoke <package>/bin/j2 --version and render
                         JSON plus each enabled optional data format.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           python-cli-runtime-and-entrypoint-contract
rec_description:        Replace imp.load_source with importlib.util.spec_from_file_location/module_from_spec/exec_module;
                         update removed ConfigParser methods; avoid incidental setuptools imports; run upstream tests and a real
                         installed executable consumer test under the target interpreter.
rec_command:            python3 -m unittest <upstream test module>; <package>/bin/j2 --version; <package>/bin/j2 --format=json <template> <data>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               python-compat-patch-and-installed-cli-test

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      pin-supported-python-runtime
fallback_description:   If upstream APIs cannot be patched safely, constrain the recipe to a runtime version that still provides
                         the required API and document the restriction; this postpones rather than resolves the migration.
fallback_command:       package metadata and Conan settings must enforce the documented Python runtime constraint
fallback_auto_fix:     false
fallback_impl:         runtime-version-constraint

forbid_1_pattern:       import imp|imp\.load_source|pkg_resources\.get_distribution|tests/render-test\.py.*without.*j2
forbid_1_reason:        These patterns leave the package dependent on removed or undeclared Python APIs, or test only source imports
                         without exercising the published console_scripts contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   Python 3.12+ can fail at import/runtime, or the advertised CLI can be missing, return an incorrect exit code,
                         or fail to resolve required runtime modules even when the unit suite passes.

principles:             R34, R51
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E319, E424, E428]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

